The choice of a defender offers every defender the combat names, whatever the range (Commander
Duels v0.9.8). King's Table.

Reason: the owner's report from the campaign's court. Liliana's Contract made both of the other
King's Generals lose at the player's upkeep (801.16: a win by an effect makes the opponents in
range lose), and in that turn's combat neither the other King nor his planeswalker could be chosen
to attack. The combat had named both as defenders: patch 0011's attack rules (Game.attackablePlayers)
let a King attack the other King once one of that King's Generals is out, across range. But when an
attacker has more than one possible defender, HumanPlayer asks with a TargetDefender, and that
target took its candidates from TargetPermanentOrPlayer: the players in the attacking player's
range of influence and the permanents of players in that range. Range is set as a turn begins
(801.2c), so it still ended at the Generals, and the choice came up empty; the attack could not be
declared. With one defender HumanPlayer asks nothing, so only a King with a planeswalker or a
battle, or one named beside other defenders, could not be chosen: the faraway King under the house
rule without its guard, too, since v0.8.7. TargetDefender now keeps the defenders it was made
with and offers each one still there (a player in the game, a permanent on the battlefield and
phased in) that its filter matches. In every other game the defenders are already those in the
attacking player's range, so the choice is the same there. Applies after 0012, which narrows the
defenders to those the attacker can attack before the choice is asked.
Upstream: none.
Remove when: XMage's TargetDefender offers the combat's defenders without asking for range again.

